Z||000000||Ronen||05-23-2001||06:56 PM||||On the spare Fiero GT V6 85 I just received there is a rear wing, which I took off for immediate safekeeping. My question is: how do I know if it is an original wing or an after market?||||reg||5
Z||000001||PBJ||05-23-2001||06:59 PM||||I have been told original wings, on the underside of the wing there should be two groves going down the length of it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||05-23-2001||07:01 PM||||Also, most aftermarket wings have molded-in stanchions, but the OEM wings have separate ones held in place with screws.||||reg||1
Z||000003||cadaver||05-23-2001||11:29 PM||||also the after market wings are fiberglass. While the real one is plastic.||||reg||1
